    fixture arms: the clean board prints orphan_count=0, the orphan fixture prints
    orphan_count=1 naming CF-009. Distinct from CF-067 (unresolvable digests) and CF-144
    (fingerprint instruments), so it is not a split closure of either.
    
    docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md gained one dated delta line naming tip a5be9c9; earlier snapshots
    were not rewritten. The CF-099 drift probe prints OK at this tip.
    
    The published tip moved six commits during the pass (a5be9c9 -> a9453d9: five events and the
    CF-176 closure). The landing was rebased rather than force-pushed: the upstream events.jsonl was
    taken whole (291 events) and this tick's own task_created line re-appended as event 292 -- its
    pre-rebase id 287 was already taken by a sibling's verification addendum. tasks.jsonl merged
    insert-only: CF-181 once, 155 rows, no duplicate ids, every line re-parsing.
    
    A second rebase was needed when CF-159's escaping fix landed as 8b81369 and added selftest section
    36; the CF-099 probe compares the plan's section count against the working tree, so it went red on
    the sibling's landing (not on this diff). Reconciled by re-measuring the plan's current-state line at
    that tip -- 36 sections, 38 arms with 4b/7b, 119 PASS rows, 19 fixture FAIL rows, board 154 rows /
    291 events -- and naming section 36 with its board row, rather than trimming the tree back.
    
    Gates at the landing tree (8b81369 + these lines):
      bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (3 warning(s), pre-existing)
      bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (rc 0), 119 PASS rows, 19 fixture FAIL rows,
        PASS 155/155 rows parse, loadavg 8.01 (1 min)
      bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh -> rc 0, agree at the landing tip
    
    This clone installs no hooks, so the GitReins guard is not silently skipped by a hook --
    it is simply not invoked on a board-and-docs-only commit (CF-031 owns that refusal class);
    the guard battery runs through gitreins task complete on this same tree.
    
