rge-base --is-ancestor 1dfb58b8aac966fa858e274992e01bad27d0632b origin/main` exits 1 while `git merge-base --is-ancestor 1232f7a04ce8bcfa94fd46166b3f05f1d1c55ffc origin/main` exits 0, and `jq -r .commit .gitreins/history/2026-11-03/410022a2/verdict.json` prints the first SHA while `jq -r 'select(.id==\"CF-077\").commit_hash' .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl` prints the second.\n2. The instrument's red arm is run, not assumed: `python3 docs/audits/cf181-verdict-binding-sweep.py . docs/audits/fixtures/cf181-board-clean.jsonl HEAD` prints `orphan_count=0` while the same command with `docs/audits/fixtures/cf181-board-orphan.jsonl` prints exactly one ORPHANED line naming `CF-009` and `orphan_count=1`.\n3. One repair direction is chosen and executed: either re-judge CF-077 so a verdict whose envelope commit is an ancestor of origin/main is appended as a new evidence entry (the historical entry stays), or the existing PASS is documented as standing on patch equivalence with the measured `git diff 1dfb58b8 1232f7a0` cited — and after either, the sweep at the fixed tip prints `orphan_count=0`.\n4. `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` and `bash tests/selftest.sh` exits 0 at the landing commit.","probe":"python3 docs/audits/cf181-verdict-binding-sweep.py . .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl origin/main"}
